t \\\\ -\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-X| & =0.4t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited growth equation, we have $3-X>0$ for all $t\\ge 0.$\nNext, we solve for $X(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-X & ={e}^{-0.4t-C} \\\\ 3-X & ={e}^{-C}{e}^{-0.4t} \\\\ 3-X & =K{e}^{-0.4t} \\\\ X & =3-K{e}^{-0.4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{-C}$ is a constant of integration.\n\nWe're told that the initial volume was $1.5\\,\\text{L}.$ So, we apply the initial condition $X(0)=1.5,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1.5 & =3-K{e}^{0} \\\\ 1.5 & =3-K \\\\ K & =1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\nX(t)=3-1.5{e}^{-0.4t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, let ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the volume is $2\\,\\text{L}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X({t}_{1}) & =2 \\\\ 3-1.5{e}^{-0.4{t}_{1}} & =2 \\\\ 1 & =1.5{e}^{-0.4{t}_{1}} \\\\ {e}^{-0.4{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -0.4{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{0.4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =1.013… \\\\  & ≈1\\,\\text{minute},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139535835 true] [17592186369106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369107 13194139535835 true] [17592186369106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369108 13194139535835 true] [17592186369106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369109 13194139535835 true] [17592186369106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369110 13194139535835 true] [17592186369106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369111 13194139535835 true] [17592186369106 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535835 true] [17592186369106 1041 "selection" 13194139535835 true] [17592186369106 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369108 13194139535835 true] [17592186369106 1110 #uuid "fdb18c16-9cae-5b03-a649-2f26b297d661" 13194139535835 true] [17592186369107 1034 "$5$ minutes" 13194139535835 true] [17592186369107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535835 true] [17592186369107 1111 #uuid "556df5ed-b540-58fd-b44a-adb7ddad3eb2" 13194139535835 true] [1759218636