matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" 13194139535835 true] [17592186369140 1113 #uuid "b03e0038-023a-5069-84d1-998d6d535a68" 13194139535835 true] [17592186369140 1145 "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535835 true] [17592186369141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369142 13194139535835 true] [17592186369141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369143 13194139535835 true] [17592186369141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369144 13194139535835 true] [17592186369141 1000 #edb/ref 1759